index 0000000..27eb2b7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/CUSTOM_DOG_TRAINING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Custom Dog Training
+
+The corrected description is loaded from:
+
+```text
+/home/hsc/custom_dog_description/urdf/custom_dog.urdf
+```
+
+The URDF contains 17 links, 16 joints, 12 actuated joints, and a total mass
+of 13.84916 kg.  The mass values are the SolidWorks assembly values supplied
+by the user: base 6.55 kg, each hip 0.65268 kg, each thigh 1.00599 kg, each
+calf 0.11021 kg, and each foot 0.05591 kg.
+
+After accepting the NVIDIA Omniverse EULA, run:
+
+```bash
+cd /home/hsc/unitree_rl_lab
+source activate_env.sh
+export OMNI_KIT_ACCEPT_EULA=YES
+./train_custom_dog_smoke.sh
+```
+
+The smoke run uses one environment and one PPO iteration.  It must create a
+training directory and `model_0.pt`.  A longer WSL run uses CPU PhysX and the
+CUDA device for PPO:
+
+```bash
+cd /home/hsc/unitree_rl_lab
+source activate_env.sh
+export OMNI_KIT_ACCEPT_EULA=YES
+CUSTOM_DOG_NUM_ENVS=128 CUSTOM_DOG_MAX_ITERATIONS=5000 \
+  ./train_custom_dog_wsl_gpu.sh
+```
+
+The custom asset starts at a base height of 0.324 m with all four thigh
+joints at 0.8 rad.  Articulation self-collisions are disabled because the
+current CAD visual meshes overlap around adjacent joint housings; ground
+contacts and illegal base contacts remain enabled.
+
+Export a policy from a checkpoint:
+
+```bash
+./export_custom_dog_policy.sh /absolute/path/to/model_N.pt
+```
+
+The custom actuator configuration models GO-M8010-6 directly on hip/thigh
+and reflects the calf 1:2 transmission by halving speed and doubling output
+torque.  Do not send an exported policy to hardware until encoder zero,
+direction, limits, RS485 IDs, emergency stop, and PD gains are calibrated.
